{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031839-more-than-ephemeral-the-abyss","id":1031839,"title":"More than ephemeral? the abyss?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-14T15:11:23-08:00","id":1031839,"title":"More than ephemeral? the abyss?","content":"So I had an NPC's casting cause an abyssal entity come through. I haven't put much of any work into this entity yet. Is there anything I should do or know to ensure it's flavored appropriately with the abyss? anything that's different from other ephemeral entities? does physical manifestation work differently? do they enter twilight? 2e core seems moderately sparse on details...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:36:57-08:00","id":1031849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031839-more-than-ephemeral-the-abyss#post1031839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I had an NPC's casting cause an abyssal entity come through. I haven't put much of any work into this entity yet. Is there anything I should do or know to ensure it's flavored appropriately with the abyss? anything that's different from other ephemeral entities? does physical manifestation work differently? do they enter twilight? 2e core seems moderately sparse on details...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gulmoth behave as spirits mechanically, Acamoth behave as Goetia mechanically.<br /> <br /> I might have that backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:13:43-08:00","id":1031867,"title":"","content":"No, you have that right.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4046\" data-vbnamecard=\"4046\">xenoterracide</a> Keep in mind though that those rules are a mechanical shortcut. You could for instance have a Gulmoth that's stuck in the Materialized Manifestation regardless of local Conditions and it's a monster that runs amok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:40:22-08:00","id":1032378,"title":"","content":"The best rule for the Abyss is not that much rule. I personally like the Abyss as the Weirdest Thing In Existence, as far as we can say that it exist.<br /> <br /> Just think of something that would somehow challenge the logic of your players. You can borrow or twist the rules on anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:16:06-08:00","id":1032395,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is really strange. Whatever comes out of it, it isn't anything that already exists. As such, you can make it pretty much act however you want. The rules say to model them as a spirit, but they don't (have to) act or exist like a spirit does. They don't even need to seem intelligent. An Abyssal manifestation might simply be a blue flame that consumes concrete and which can't be put out by any of the usual means (water, smothering, a Forces spell, etc.). It doesn't burn flesh, so it isn't a threat immediately, except until the room the Mages are in starts to crumble to ash, and keeps spreading. Suddenly, we've got a violation of the Lex spreading through the area. The PCs either need to fix it fast or destroy the evidence and get the hell out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:31:18-08:00","id":1032789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031839-more-than-ephemeral-the-abyss#post1031839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything I should do or know to ensure it's flavored appropriately with the abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. In fact, Abyss defies description and flavor. Just make it as creepy, confusing and weird as you can. My favorite abyss spirit so far was anti-magical &quot;robot&quot; who infected, consumed and fused cars and their spirits into weird spirit-mechanical monstrosities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}